title AMUS15 — Constel catch-up: a lagging pier brought current from a leader's snapshot + tail
prompt Read REMEMBER and the two road-ahead design docs; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve own design rounds and make progress before checking in; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61; STOP at custody gates.
think Read REMEMBER via targeted greps (huge, long-line), the 1,024-round itinerary, and the six-season double-seat expansion. REMEMBER's living-edge paragraph names CAUM6 yet the true living edge is the Constel AMUS ladder (Season D thread) — git log and the newest session logs run AMUS10..AMUS14, latest commit AMUS14 snapshot. Confirmed by reading constel/README and the AMUS14 log.
think The README road-on names the socket as the one rung crossing the Comlink seam (real file descriptor) — a custody gate, not agent-doable. So the crux is the hardest still-tractable PURE rung.
think Lindy-first crux-first among pure rungs: CATCH-UP. AMUS14 built the snapshot; the reason a real system compacts at all is the pier that fell behind. A follower too far behind to replay must INSTALL the snapshot — Raft's InstallSnapshot — which spends AMUS14's work directly rather than accreting a new concern beside it. It is the single hardest-but-tractable pure move left, and it composes AMUS12 log + AMUS14 snapshot over their public shapes. Self-approved the design round.
think Design: a follower lacks effective entries [follower.total(), leader.total()); the leader can serve an index only at or past leader.snap.count. So the follower's position chooses the method. Tail catch-up (follower.total() >= snap.count): serve the missing tail live, verifying the overlap (follower.effective_state() == leader_state_at(follower.total())) before a single append so a divergent follower is refused whole. Snapshot install (follower.total() < snap.count): adopt the leader's snapshot wholesale, empty the tail, take the leader's whole live tail — trust-the-snapshot by AMUS14's identity property. Every non-refusing catch_up ends with follower.equivalent(leader) asserted.
obs Built constel/catchup.rye GREEN on the first build; witness tools/amus_catchup_witness.rish GREEN. Eight selftest blocks: tail catch-up appends and reads back; snapshot install reaches a follower far below a compacted leader's boundary; already-current returns 0 untouched; a divergent overlap refuses Diverged unchanged (the check is real); a longer follower refuses Ahead; NO FORK across catch-up (two followers caught up from one leader equivalent to each other and to the leader, then advancing with the sky and staying equivalent); bounded past max_tail; a real decree-built sky drives it end to end.
obs TAME style check clean (bans clean; ratchet counts printed). Every fn holds >=2 asserts with // invariant: lines; opening triad std/assert/print; snake_case; named errors (CatchupError = {Ahead, Diverged} || SnapshotError); bounded (the follower auto-compacts, tail_len <= max_tail throughout); no @memcpy. Prior AMUS rungs stay GREEN (additive); baseline amus_snapshot_witness re-run GREEN before starting.
obs Docs kept synced in the same round: constel/README.md gains the AMUS15 catchup rung entry, the run-block line, the Status ladder, the Kin design-doc link, and the road-on now naming recovery as the sixth proven property (identity, value, order, membership, endurance, recovery).
obs Custody-first held: purely local, no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real address ever formed. Custody gate #2 (real hardware / any real wire) and gate #4 (real Kumara) untouched. The socket rung stays the maintainer's hand — no gate crossed this lap. REMEMBER's living-edge paragraph is stale (names CAUM6); only its Git nib is refreshed this round, the full CAUM->AMUS living-edge rewrite left as its own remember pass rather than folded into a mechanical lap.
obs Clock note: America/New_York read 20260814.061337, earlier than the prior newest 083000; the one-clock monotonic law honored by stamping 083200, just after the work it follows.
